This is a confirmed, known, recurring issue — not a new bug.

**Root cause:** Live `evetest eve app-info passthrough-app` on the paused device shows the `passthrough-app` once `RUNNING` with `assignedAdapters:{...name:"ethernet1"...}` (the directly-assigned passthrough NIC) plus exactly 4 `network:{}` entries (`vif0`, `newvif1`, `newvif2`, `newvif3`) — the passthrough adapter never appears as a `network` entry, matching the test's observed `len:4` vs expected `5`. This is caused by `pkg/pillar/cmd/zedagent/handlemetrics.go`, where the `Network` list is built only from `aiStatus.GetAppInterfaceList()` (virtual VIFs, line 1219) while `IoAdapterList`/passthrough adapters (line 1190) only populate `AssignedAdapters`. Master has the fix in commit `979ea453c` ("zedagent: report passthrough NICs in app info and metrics"), which I confirmed via `git merge-base --is-ancestor` is **not** present on this `17.0-stable` branch. Per the ledger, this exact failure (and its sibling `TestNetworkAdapterPassthroughChange`) has been recurring every night since 2026-11-17 — it's a missing backport, not a new regression or flake.

